   "subject": "Re: [r-inla] Using Spatio-temporal Bayesian hierarchical with INLA with longitude and latitude",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi,<div>you need the files in the R folder of the zip file linked to at the end of the <a href=\"http://www.r-inla.org/spde-book\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.r-inla.org/spde-book&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792440500812000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3-O4-SBRm87NO-dfapdg55\">http://www.r-inla.org/spde-book</a> page.</div><div>You need to click the download arrow at the far right side of the page.</div><div><br></div><div>Finn</div></div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gmail_attr\">On Tue, 25 Aug 2020 at 20:39, Taghreed alghamdi &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">taghreed....@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:<br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><font size=\"2\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana,sans-serif\">I checked the gitbook version of this book&quot;<span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-style:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-color:initial\">Advanced Spatial Modeling with Stochastic Partial Differential Equations Using R and INLA&quot;</span> in the link you posted. <br></span></font></div><div><font size=\"2\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana,sans-serif\">In chapter 7, when I use this code</span></font></div><div><font size=\"2\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana,sans-serif\"><br></span></font></div><div><pre><code><a rel=\"nofollow\">x.k &lt;-<span> </span><span>book.rspde</span>(coords, <span>range =</span> <span>sqrt</span>(<span>8</span>) <span>/</span><span> </span>params[<span>2</span>], </a>\r\n<a rel=\"nofollow\">  <span>sigma =</span> <span>sqrt</span>(params[<span>1</span>]), <span>n =</span> k, <span>mesh =</span> prmesh1,</a>\r\n  <span>return.attributes =</span> <span>TRUE</span>)<br><br><span style=\"font-family:verdana,sans-serif\"><font size=\"2\">I get error message </font></span><span style=\"color:rgb(204,0,0)\">&quot;Error in book.rspde(coords, range = sqrt(8)/params[2], sigma = sqrt(params[1]),  : <br>  could not find function &quot;book.rspde&quot;</span><br><br><span style=\"font-family:verdana,sans-serif\">I tried to install all libraries and packages I could ever think of, but I still get the same error message. <br>Any help please regarding this error?</span><br><br></code></pre></div><div><br></div><br>On Tuesday, July 28, 2020 at 7:56:35 PM UTC-4, Elias T. Krainski wrote:</div></blockquote></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div>\r\n    <p>Yes. You can check examples on the following links:</p>\r\n    <p><a href=\"http://www.r-inla.org/examples/tutorials/spde-tutorial-from-jss\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.r-inla.org/examples/tutorials/spde-tutorial-from-jss&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792440500812000&amp;usg=AOvVaw26JlwDhtCirljZt4bID5lN\">http://www.r-inla.org/examples/tutorials/spde-tutorial-from-jss</a></p>\r\n    <p><a href=\"https://haakonbakka.bitbucket.io/organisedtopics.html\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://haakonbakka.bitbucket.io/organisedtopics.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792440500812000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3biKq9WZoLfIbDJN4zkxvt\">https://haakonbakka.bitbucket.io/organisedtopics.html</a> (Stream 3)<br>\r\n    </p>\r\n    <p><a href=\"http://www.r-inla.org/spde-book\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.r-inla.org/spde-book&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792440500812000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3-O4-SBRm87NO-dfapdg55\">http://www.r-inla.org/spde-book</a></p>\r\n    <p>Elias<br>\r\n    </p>\r\n    <div>On 28/07/2020 20:08, Taghreed alghamdi\r\n      wrote:<br>\r\n    </div>\r\n    </div></blockquote></div></blockquote></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div><blockquote type=\"cite\">\r\n      \r\n      <div dir=\"ltr\">\r\n        <div>I&#39;m currently doing my research on Spatio-temporal Bayesian\r\n          hierarchical with INLA to predict traffic flow.</div>\r\n        <div>My data contains time, traffic flow, longitude, and\r\n          latitude. <br>\r\n        </div>\r\n        <div><br>\r\n        </div>\r\n        <div>Just wanted to confirm if INLA deals with spatial point as\r\n          longitude, and latitude or it just handles polygons spatial\r\n          data?</div>\r\n        <div>Most of the examples you provide on the page have a\r\n          location as polygons spatial data.</div>\r\n        <div><br>\r\n        </div>\r\n        <div>Also, can I do prediction or it&#39;s only more suitable for\r\n          analysis?<br>\r\n        </div>\r\n        <div>I tried to check the code of the examples you have but I\r\n          can&#39;t find a sample one that applies on data with longitude,\r\n          and latitude</div>\r\n        <div><br>\r\n        </div>\r\n        <div>\r\n          <pre style=\"margin:0px 0px 1em;padding:12px 8px;border:0px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;font-stretch:inherit;line-height:inherit;font-family:Consolas,Menlo,Monaco,&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,&quot;DejaVu Sans Mono&quot;,&quot;Bitstream Vera Sans Mono&quot;,&quot;Courier New&quot;,monospace,sans-serif;font-size:13px;vertical-align:baseline;width:auto;max-height:600px;overflow:auto;border-radius:3px;display:block;color:rgb(36,39,41);letter-spacing:normal;text-align:left;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;word-spacing:0px\"><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px\"><code><div><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">ID latitude longitude </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,0,102)\">Time</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,0,102)\">Traffic_Flow</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">1</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">43.94834</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">-</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">78.85344</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">2020</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">-</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">06</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">-</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">01</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">06</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">:</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">00</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">33</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">2</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">41.91904</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">-</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">87.63961</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">2020</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">-</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">06</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">-</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">01</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">06</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">:</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">00</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">52</span></div></code></div><cod